{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:26-2","provision":"BCO 26-2","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"26-2","title":"Section 26-2","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/26-2/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/26-2","current_text":{"html":"<p>Amendments to the <i>Book of Church Order</i> may be made only in the following manner: 1. Approval of the proposed amendment by majority of those present and voting in the General Assembly, and its recommendation to the Presbyteries. 2. The advice and consent of two-thirds (2/3) of the Presbyteries. 3. The approval and enactment by a subsequent General Assembly by a majority of those present and voting.</p>","text":"Amendments to the Book of Church Order may be made only in the following manner: 1. Approval of the proposed amendment by majority of those present and voting in the General Assembly, and its recommendation to the Presbyteries. 2. The advice and consent of two-thirds (2/3) of the Presbyteries. 3. The approval and enactment by a subsequent General Assembly by a majority of those present and voting."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"14d73f7e5caf1d22e0514870dd30fcc69f8165cc","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"38e35af46c8cbdb12a9a00c82d72f7192575b5ec27348534148f2a834551edc4","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudic